sequenceDiagram
    actor C as Citizen (browser)
    participant P as Citizen / NIS Portal (SPA)
    participant KC as Keycloak — citizens realm
    participant API as citizen-backend :4100
    participant SA as Keycloak Admin API<br/>(citizen-provisioning-service)
    participant DB as PostgreSQL (appdb)

    Note over C,KC: 1 — Login once (Authorization Code + PKCE)
    C->>P: open Citizen Portal :3000
    P->>KC: /authorize (client=citizen-portal, PKCE S256)
    C->>KC: credentials
    KC-->>P: authorization code
    P->>KC: /token (code + PKCE verifier)
    KC-->>P: access + refresh token<br/>(iss=citizens, role CITIZEN)
    Note right of KC: realm SSO session cookie set

    Note over C,KC: 2 — Navigate to NIS portal (silent SSO, no re-login)
    C->>P: open NIS Portal :3002
    P->>KC: /authorize (client=nis-portal)
    KC-->>P: silent code (existing SSO session)
    P->>KC: /token
    KC-->>P: token (aud=citizen-api)

    Note over C,DB: 3 — Gate: is this citizen enrolled in NIS?
    P->>API: GET /api/me (Bearer)
    API->>KC: validate JWT offline (JWKS, iss/aud/azp)
    API->>DB: SELECT nis_members WHERE sub
    DB-->>API: none
    API-->>P: { nisEnrolled: false }
    P-->>C: show "NIS registration required"

    Note over C,DB: 4 — Enrolment (backend-mediated, self only)
    C->>P: submit NIS registration form
    P->>API: POST /api/nis/enrol (Bearer)
    API->>API: validate token + zod input; enrol token.sub only
    API->>DB: INSERT nis_members (allocated NIS number)
    API->>SA: client_credentials → admin token
    API->>SA: grant realm role NIS_MEMBER to sub
    API->>DB: INSERT citizen_audit_events
    API-->>P: { nisNumber }

    Note over C,DB: 5 — Token refresh picks up the new role → services unlocked
    P->>KC: refresh token (force)
    KC-->>P: new access token incl. NIS_MEMBER
    P->>API: GET /api/nis/contributions (Bearer)
    API->>API: require NIS_MEMBER + ownership by sub
    API->>DB: SELECT own record only
    DB-->>API: contributions
    API-->>P: data
    P-->>C: NIS dashboard
